<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Taghlib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 979</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Taghlib was the Hamdanid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> who deposed his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-al-dawla">Nasir al-Dawla</a> in 967. He became entangled in the struggles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyid dynasty</a>, backing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izz-al-dawla">Izz al-Dawla</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adud-al-dawla">Adud al-Dawla</a>. In 978 Adud al-Dawla expelled him from Mosul, and he was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> in 979 while fighting forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>.</p></div>
